+ Got Python code from Google search AI and, after modified so that it
  actually runs, plus addition so that it renders the complete surface 
  (not just the "spectral pulses", but also their complements;  thanks
  ChatGPT) is generating a reasonable surface

  ./cie-spectral-solid-boundary.py


+ {gMOIP} package has inHull() for determining point inside convex hull
  of other points

  Can use geometry::convhulln() to only generate convex hull once
  (to send to inHull())/


